From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: image list effects, scaling and IImageList2

ImageList_DrawIndirect ignored ILS_GLOW, ILS_SHADOW, ILD_SCALE and
ILD_DPISCALE (FIXMEs); IImageList2's Resize, GetOriginalSize,
SetOriginalSize, SetCallback, GetCallback, ForceImagePresent,
DiscardImages, PreloadImages, GetStatistics, Replace2 and
ReplaceFromImageList were E_NOTIMPL; ImageList_WriteEx was a semi-stub
and ImageList_ReadEx was missing.

- ILS_GLOW draws the image's silhouette, spread two pixels, in crEffect
  (the highlight colour by default) under the image; ILS_SHADOW draws it
  two pixels down and right, softened, at half strength (black by
  default). The silhouette is the image's alpha, else its mask.
- ILD_SCALE draws the image to the cx by cy asked for (with its blend,
  saturation, alpha and overlay) instead of clipping it; ILD_DPISCALE to
  the destination's DPI.
- IImageList2: Resize stretches every image to the new size and keeps
  them; original sizes are kept per image (following removals);
  SetCallback/GetCallback; the images are always present, so
  ForceImagePresent, DiscardImages and PreloadImages succeed for valid
  images; GetStatistics (allocated, used, none on standby); Replace2;
  ReplaceFromImageList copies another list's image with its
  transparency.
- ImageList_WriteEx checks its flags (ILP_NORMAL, ILP_DOWNLEVEL);
  ImageList_ReadEx reads a list and returns the interface asked for.

Wine's comctl32 imagelist tests: 10023 tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/imglist2-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/imglist2-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_EFFECTS, SG_MUTANT_NO_SCALE (comctl32/imagelist.c).
